.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH kakashi 1  "kakashi 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
kakashi \- Kakashi — the ELCI deterministic system replication & equivalence engine (§1). See `docs/` for the full architectural directive
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBkakashi\fR [\fB\-\-state\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Kakashi — the ELCI deterministic system replication & equivalence engine (§1). See `docs/` for the full architectural directive
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fI<STATE>\fR [default: .]
Directory containing (or to contain) the `.kakashi/` state directory (§34)
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: human]

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
kakashi\-init(1)
Create the `.kakashi/` state directory and an initial manifest
.TP
kakashi\-inspect(1)
Stage A static discovery of a reference tree
.TP
kakashi\-fingerprint(1)
Compute deterministic fingerprints for a tree (§22)
.TP
kakashi\-characterise(1)
Stage A + Stage B: static discovery plus CLI surface extraction
.TP
kakashi\-observe(1)
Run one confined invocation of `program` and record it as an experiment (§6, §13)
.TP
kakashi\-probe(1)
Stage D boundary probing of `program` (§23, §24)
.TP
kakashi\-model(1)
Assemble a system model from previously recorded discovery, fingerprint, and ELCI adapter health (§35, §36)
.TP
kakashi\-replicate(1)
Produce a replication brief (§37, §46) — evidence for the next proposal step, not a replica
.TP
kakashi\-diff(1)
Structural (and, if probe records are given, behavioural) differential comparison of two trees (§25)
.TP
kakashi\-validate(1)
Score measured equivalence dimensions and report a gate PASS/FAIL disposition (§26, §41)
.TP
kakashi\-converge(1)
Run one convergence iteration and append it to the ledger (§38, §39)
.TP
kakashi\-report(1)
Render the executive/machine\-readable report (§41)
.TP
kakashi\-replay(1)
Re\-run a recorded experiment from its manifest and check for reproducibility (§32)
.TP
kakashi\-export(1)
Copy the evidence graph, models, reports, and differences out of `.kakashi/` into a portable directory
.TP
kakashi\-status(1)
Summarise manifest, evidence counts, and ELCI adapter health
.TP
kakashi\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
